		C. Incorrect. Anxiety about information does not automatically make treatment impossible.
		D. Correct. The therapist should pace and adapt the discussion while still providing material information.
		CTA Exam Strategy: Do not overwhelm—but do not materially mislead.
		Remediation: Return to Workbook 1, Chapter 2: Information Required for Informed Decision-Making; review Client Request to Avoid Material Information; log error category INFORMATION-DISCLOSURE.',
