		'question_text'  => 'A 14-year-old is brought to therapy by an aunt. The aunt pays for the intake and states:“The child’s mother knows I am helping.”The aunt is not a legal guardian, no parent has authorized treatment, and the therapist has not yet determined whether the minor may consent independently.What should the therapist do first?',
		'option_a'       => 'Begin treatment because the aunt is a close relative and is paying',
