	array(
		'question_text'  => 'A current custody order grants the parents joint legal custody and expressly states that both parents must consent before the child begins nonemergency mental-health treatment.One parent signs the treatment consent. The other parent objects. No emergency is present, and the therapist has not determined that the minor qualifies to consent independently.What is the therapist’s most appropriate response?',
