	array(
		'question_text'  => 'A current order grants the parents joint legal custody. It requires mutual consent for major surgery and international travel but permits either parent to act alone in other healthcare matters.The mother authorizes ordinary outpatient therapy. After treatment begins, the father objects and demands immediate termination. No safety emergency is present, and the treatment does not conflict with the physical-custody order.What is the strongest analysis?',
