		This creates a potential legal basis for treatment without prior authorization from a parent or guardian. The therapist must still evaluate the statutory requirements and document the clinical and legal basis for proceeding.
		A. Incorrect. The statutory minimum age is 12, not 10. A request for confidentiality alone does not establish authority to consent.
		C. Incorrect. Emancipated minors may possess broader consent rights, but emancipation is not required under these particular minor-consent statutes.
