		C. Incorrect. California law expressly allows some minors aged 12 or older to consent independently.
		D. Incorrect. A teacher may provide useful contextual information when disclosure is authorized, but the statute places the maturity determination with the attending professional.
		CTA Exam Strategy: Distinguish: Old enough to be consideredfrommature enough to consent Age is objective. Maturity requires an individualized professional determination.
