	array(
		'question_text'  => 'A minor was removed from a parent’s physical custody through dependency proceedings. The parent later presents a juvenile court order authorizing access to the minor’s mental-health records. After an individualized good-faith assessment, the therapist determines that access would seriously damage the professional relationship and adversely affect the minor’s psychological well-being. What is the strongest analysis?',
		'option_a'       => 'The therapist must release the records because any court authorization eliminates all professional judgment',
